--!       only when its body is strict, and `x AND y` is not, so STRICT would
--!       stop inlining. Inlined, the planner sees two comparisons on
--!       `{{ schema }}.{{ b.extractor }}(a)`, which a btree index on that expression
--!       serves as one range scan.{% if b.ore %} For this ORE range that index needs the
